From 5eaaf25908568b919066eb37dcae2cf4377240b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dandan Wu <wudandan@kylinos.cn>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 07:39:10 +0800
Subject: [PATCH v5 16/31] ntfs: report attribute resize and relocation
 recovery failures

Resize can fail after changing allocation or record placement without
reporting the resulting state. Report failed recovery and missing
required attributes, preserving allocation errors and using
EFSCORRUPTED for confirmed corruption.

After a nonresident shrink, report context or lookup failures when the
old data size exceeds the shortened allocation.
Track moves in resident resize and attribute-list mapping updates.
Report interrupted changes and failed list persistence unless the
updater already reported that error, including resident resize. Preserve
resize and relocation errnos; keep early allocation failures distinct.

Signed-off-by: Dandan Wu <wudandan@kylinos.cn>
---
Additional V5 validation:
- Forty-five extracted-source scenarios cover resident resize,
  attribute-list mapping updates, and lowest-VCN list persistence,
  including failures before and after record moves, successful resize,
  and avoiding duplicate lower-level reports. Original errnos
  are preserved; early allocation failures do not cause recovery
  reports.
- These are userspace tests with controlled dependencies and
  ASan/UBSan, not kernel fault-injection tests.

Resident-resize reporting validation:
- Twenty-four additional extracted-source cases exercise both
  relocation paths with six errnos and lower-level reporting on/off.
- Twelve cases reported the same failure twice before this fix.
  All 82 relocation cases pass after the fix under ASan/UBSan.
- Controlled dependencies check local flow and errno preservation;
  these tests do not validate kernel event delivery.

